## 🌐 Web Exploitation

**Browser DevTools** (press `F12`): inspect HTML, JavaScript, cookies (Application/Storage tab), and network requests (Network tab).

```bash
curl http://target/               # Fetch a page
curl -i http://target/            # -i also shows the response headers
curl -v http://target/            # -v verbose: shows request and response details
curl -X POST -d "user=a&pass=b" http://target/login   # Send a POST request with form data
curl -H "Header-Name: value" http://target/           # Send a custom header
curl -b "session=abc123" http://target/               # Send a cookie
```

Useful files to check on authorized web challenges:

- `view-source:` in the browser (the page's raw HTML)
- `/robots.txt` (paths the site asks crawlers to avoid)
- HTML comments and linked JavaScript files

**Directory discovery** (only when the CTF explicitly allows it):

```bash
gobuster dir -u http://target/ -w wordlist.txt   # Try paths from a wordlist to find hidden pages
ffuf -u http://target/FUZZ -w wordlist.txt       # Similar: FUZZ is replaced by each word
```

**Burp Suite** (Community Edition) lets you intercept and edit requests between your browser and an in-scope target.

