## 🖼️ Steganography

Steganography means hiding data inside other files (images, audio, etc.).

```bash
exiftool image.jpg                # Check metadata and comments first
strings image.jpg | tail          # Look for text appended to the end of the file
file image.png                    # Confirm the file type
xxd image.jpg | head              # Check the header bytes
binwalk image.jpg                 # Detect embedded files
binwalk -e image.jpg              # Extract embedded files
steghide info image.jpg           # Check whether a JPEG has embedded data (may ask for a passphrase)
steghide extract -sf image.jpg    # Extract hidden data (-sf = stego file); use only a passphrase given by the challenge
zsteg image.png                   # Check PNG/BMP files for common LSB hiding patterns
pngcheck image.png                # Validate PNG structure and spot oddities
```

Also try: viewing the image at different zoom levels, checking color channels in an image editor, and reading the challenge description for hints about passwords.

