## 🌍 OSINT

OSINT = Open Source Intelligence: finding information from **public** sources.

> ⚖️ In a CTF, stay inside the scenario you were given. Never investigate real private individuals.

```bash
whois example.com                 # Domain registration info
dig example.com                   # DNS records
dig example.com MX                # Look up a specific record type (MX = mail servers)
nslookup example.com              # Another way to look up DNS
exiftool photo.jpg                # Photos may contain location/time metadata
```

**Search operators (Google):**

```text
site:example.com keyword          # Search only within one site
filetype:pdf keyword              # Find a specific file type
intitle:"keyword"                 # Words in the page title
"exact phrase"                    # Match an exact phrase
```

**Other techniques:**
- Reverse image search (Google Lens, TinEye)
- [Wayback Machine](https://web.archive.org/) for old versions of web pages
- Note the source of every clue, and **verify using at least two independent sources**

